Robot Navigation in Smart Factory
A smart manufacturing unit uses autonomous robots to transport materials between
stations. The factory layout is represented as a graph:
Nodes: Junctions in the factory floor.
Edges: Paths between junctions, weighted by travel time (considering obstacles
and robot traffic).
A robot needs to move from Source (charging station) to Destination (assembly
point) in the shortest possible time. Obstacles and temporary congestion may change
path weights dynamically.
As a robotics engineer, you are assigned to:
1. Implement Dijkstra’s algorithm to find shortest travel path for robots.
2. Update paths dynamically if obstacles appear or paths become congested.
3. Optimize the system for large factories with hundreds or thousands of robots.
4. Provide a graphical visualization of the robot’s optimal path.
